# AI readiness (repo baseline)

When setting up a repository, joining a checkout that lacks `AGENTS.md` or
`ai-copilots/`, or answering whether a repo is AI-ready / agent-operable:

- Load `.cursor/skills/ai-readiness/SKILL.md` (checklist in `reference.md`).
- When a real scaffold fork exists and the human has not asked to implement yet,
  Read `.cursor/personas/ai-readiness.persona.md` and follow it.
- After the baseline exists, author or migrate skills with
  `.cursor/skills/author-ai-copilots/SKILL.md` and
  `.cursor/skills/agent-smith/SKILL.md`.

Every git repository agents operate MUST have root `AGENTS.md` plus
`ai-copilots/` (README, BOOTSTRAP, at least one skill). Fail closed until the
checklist passes. Library-specific recipes stay in that repo's `ai-copilots/`;
do not spill them into cursor-packs.
